<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $977 mln Dec 26.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $977 mln Dec 26.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $977 million surplus on Dec 26 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>Wednesday's surplus was due to an increase in financial buy transactions, which jumped to $1.305 billion.</p>
<p>Traders said this increase was due partly to payments by foreign investors for the purchase of a 35 percent stake in Rio Grande do Sul's telecom CRT.  </p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank</p>
<p>issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 18</p>
<p>Exports: $368 million</p>
<p>Imports: $275 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.305 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $421 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $977 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.809 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.822 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $8.812 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $5.397 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $3.402 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded .</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418))</p>
